{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"850792255224152104","content":"Staff of the Lost Land\nArtifact, staff (requires attunement from a spellcaster)\n\nMade of the intertwined roots of three ancient trees, each imbuing the staff with a separate gift. From the Hanging Tree, the dread and disease of the Uru that loitered it’s branches. From the Spellmart, the wonderment of creation and spirit of it’s proprietor, Iona. And from the Baeshra tree, the very spirit of the lizardfolk it was named after. You gain +3 to saving throws, save DC, and spell attack bonus.\n\nThe Hanging Tree: The greying decrepit root’s energy can be harnessed to cast Negative Energy Flood at a creature. If the creature is undead, roll the 5d12 damage if the damage would kill it, it crumbles to dust instead of giving it temporary hit points. You can use this once per day and it resets at the witching hour. \n\nOnce per week you can thrust the diseased spirit of the Uru upon a creature to truly Harm (DC17) them.\n\n\nThe Spellmart: The soft white root radiates with a calming and warm presence. you can press the staff to the ground and cast Circle of Power. When cast this way, the staff holds the concentration of the spell and all friendly creatures within the circle gain temporary hit points equal to their proficiency bonus. You can use this once per day and it resets at dawn.\n\nOnce per week, at your bequest, can extend and solidify it’s warm presence into a Globe of Invulnerability. \n\nThe Baeshra Tree: The hearty roots of the Baeshra tree are brimming with wild and ancient powers. By your will these powers can surge into you and you become a Guardian of Nature. When cast this way the staff holds the concentration the Guardian forms get the following changes:\nPrimal Beast: Your appearance becomes more lizard like and the bonus damage die becomes a d8.\nGreat Tree: The temporary hit points refresh each turn, as long as the spell is active.\nYou can use this once per day and it resets at dusk.\n\nOnce per week you can wield the power of the Baeshra Tree to Reincarnate a deceased creature, however they only reincarnate as a Lizardfolk.\n\nThe staff can be split apart into 3 separate staves: The Hanging Staff, The Spellmart Staff, and the Baeshra Staff. When split the staves lose their ability to use their weekly ability and only give a +1 bonus to saving throws, save DC, and spell attack bonus.","created_at":"2021-08-27T01:47:57.469000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"880629681882300416","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
